{"full":"hf:Tom199328/MOSS-TTS-Nano","spaceId":"Tom199328/MOSS-TTS-Nano","name":"MOSS-TTS-Nano ONNX Demo","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":4,"created":"2026-04-19T11:26:22.000Z","updated":"2026-05-19T07:58:36.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://tom199328-moss-tts-nano.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Tom199328/MOSS-TTS-Nano","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:32:40.794Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:32:40.794Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:32:40.794Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🗣️","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["MOSS-TTS-Nano is an open-source multilingual tiny speech generation model from MOSI.AI and the OpenMOSS team. With only 0.1B parameters, it is designed for realtime speech generation, can run directly on CPU without a GPU, and keeps the deployment stack simple enough for local demos, web serving, and lightweight product integration.","MOSS-TTS-Nano focuses on the part of TTS deployment that matters most in practice: small footprint, low latency, good enough quality for realtime products, and simple local setup. It uses a pure autoregressive Audio Tokenizer + LLM pipeline and keeps the inference workflow friendly for both terminal users and web-demo users.","MOSS-Audio-Tokenizer is the unified discrete audio interface for the entire MOSS-TTS family. It is built on the Cat (Causal Audio Tokenizer with Transformer) architecture, a CNN-free audio tokenizer composed entirely of causal Transformer blocks. It serves as the shared audio backbone for MOSS-TTS, MOSS-TTS-Nano, MOSS-TTSD, MOSS-VoiceGenerator, MOSS-SoundEffect, and MOSS-TTS-Realtime, providing a consistent audio representation across the full product family."],"features":["MOSS-TTS: the flagship model for high-fidelity zero-shot voice cloning, long-speech generation, fine-grained control over Pinyin, phonemes, and duration, and multilingual/code-switched synthesis.","MOSS-TTS-Local-Transformer: a smaller model in the family based on MossTTSLocal, designed to keep the MOSS-TTS style of speech generation in a lighter model size.","MOSS-TTSD-v1.0: a spoken dialogue generation model for expressive, multi-speaker, and ultra-long dialogue audio.","MOSS-VoiceGenerator: a voice design model that can generate diverse voices and speaking styles directly from text prompts, without reference speech.","MOSS-SoundEffect: a controllable sound generation model for natural ambience, city scenes, animals, human actions, and short music-like audio fragments."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Tom199328/MOSS-TTS-Nano/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cd61a0952768ebebd1c25d143cd6d8cb0afeb59b5acf97508077e2e1bf678269","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:32:40.891Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:32:40.891Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"MOSS-TTS-Nano is an open-source multilingual tiny speech generation model from MOSI.AI and the OpenMOSS team. With only 0.1B parameters, it is designed for realtime speech generation, can run directly on CPU without a GPU, and keeps the deployment stack simple enough for local demos, web serving, and lightweight product integration.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Tom199328/MOSS-TTS-Nano/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"MOSS-TTS-Nano is an open-source multilingual tiny speech generation model from MOSI.AI and the OpenMOSS team. With only 0.1B parameters, it is designed for realtime speech generation, can run directly on CPU without a GPU, and keeps the deployment stack simple enough for local demos, web serving, and lightweight product integration.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Tom199328/MOSS-TTS-Nano/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"cd61a0952768ebebd1c25d143cd6d8cb0afeb59b5acf97508077e2e1bf6